 arning-sciences\n\nClinical Mind AI: Building an International AI Platform
  for Health Professions Education and the Learning Sciences\n\nHAI Seminar
  with Marcos Santiago Rojas Pino and Thomas Caruso\n\nVisit our website to
  learn more about the event agenda\, speakers\, and other details\n\nClini
 cal Mind AI is a Stanford-developed\, international collaborative platform
  designed to strengthen clinical reasoning education through AI-simulated 
 patient encounters across health professions. The platform enables educato
 rs to create clinical cases aligned with their local curricula\, learning 
 goals\, languages\, and assessment needs\, while giving learners repeated 
 opportunities to practice open-ended history-taking\, diagnostic reasoning
 \, and communication. The seminar will present the motivation for Clinical
  Mind AI\, its design principles\, and how the platform is being used by e
 ducators and institutions across countries to support scalable\, instructo
 r-centered clinical simulation.\n\nThe talk will also discuss Clinical Min
 d AI as a research infrastructure for studying learning in clinical reason
 ing tasks. We will describe how learner interactions with AI-simulated pat
 ients can generate interpretable evidence about reasoning processes\, incl
 uding how students gather information\, update hypotheses\, document findi
 ngs\, and respond to feedback. The seminar will focus on broader questions
  at the intersection of AI\, medical education\, and learning science: how
